Strapi Audit Logging Plugin

A comprehensive audit logging system for Strapi that automatically tracks all content changes through the Content API with detailed change tracking and flexible querying capabilities.

Architecture Overview

This plugin integrates seamlessly with Strapi's core architecture using:
Core Components
Lifecycle Hooks: Automatically captures create, update, and delete operations
Custom Content Type: Stores audit logs in dedicated `audit_logs` collection
REST API: Provides filtered querying with pagination and sorting
Role-Based Access Control: Secure access to audit data
Configuration System: Flexible enable/disable and content type exclusion


Features
Automated Audit Logging
Automatic tracking of all create, update, delete operations
Comprehensive metadata content type, record ID, action, timestamp, user
Change tracking Field-level diffs for updates, full payload for create/delete
User context Captures authenticated user information

REST API
Filter by: Content type, user, action type, date
Pagination: Limit/offset based pagination
Sorting: Multiple field sorting support

Security & Configuration
Role-based access: Only users with `read_audit_logs` permission can access
Configurable: Global enable/disable and content type exclusion
Error handling: Graceful error recovery without breaking operations
